Mapping DTO↔entity is in `OwnerMapper.java`. Note `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id`, `pets`, `customerCode`, and `householdId` (those are assigned by later pipeline steps). `toOwnerDto` computes `displayName` and `initials`. `sharesHousehold` exists only on the request DTO and is never mapped onto the entity.

## 6. Existing tests

Only acceptance tests exist (black-box, driving `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`).

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — shared base. Key helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully valid/unique owner: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`, `getOwner`, `fetchOwner`, `deleteOwner`, `structuredOwner()` (uses `addressLine1`/`postcode`), `withPostcode`, `knownOwner`, plus `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` helpers. Runs `@Transactional` (rolled back), `@WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN, VET_ADMIN, ADMIN)`.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the active checkpoint. Its class comment: *"address-normalize: Introduce address normalization applied whenever an owner is created: trim and collapse wh..."*. Test methods:
  - `coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase()` — posts `address = "  12  main  st "`, expects stored `$.address == "12 MAIN STREET"`.
  - `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations()` — posts `address = "7 elm ave"`, expects `"7 ELM AVENUE"`.
  - `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize()` — posts `address = "   "`, expects HTTP 400.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — test support for audit assertions (not owner-address specific).

